{"kind":"assert","text":"Attempted the carry Hugh authorised and backed it out. Recording what I found, because it changes the shape of 69bd36a7 from a rebase into a feature merge.\n\nI rebased the seven commits of 43daa5f0 onto current main 7e7b8412 in a scratch worktree. Four carried cleanly. Two conflicts were only the generated internal/service/uidist embed, which is regenerated from source and not merged by hand. One was real and one was disqualifying.\n\nThe real one, in RequestList.tsx, was tractable: main added a vocabulary binding while the branch lifted sort, query and population into a view prop. Both are wanted and I merged them by keeping both.\n\nThe disqualifying one is commit 75a1eb33 against main's 511335e7. The two lanes built overlapping features independently and neither knows about the other. Main renders three summary links -- reasoning moved, stale, awaiting ratification -- and carries \"awaiting ratification\" as a lifecycle state plus a ratificationRows function keyed on vocabulary, returning rows and ratifiers. The branch deletes those links and replaces them with five tabs driven by a uniform workRows(projection, context, population) over POPULATIONS = live, moved, stale, done, closed. Ratification is not one of them, and it cannot be, because it takes vocabulary and returns a different shape.\n\nResolving that hunk by taking the branch side -- the mechanical move -- silently deleted ratificationRows and the \"awaiting ratification\" state from rows.ts. That is merged main behaviour, shipped in 511335e7, and dropping it would have been a regression I introduced while claiming to carry work forward. I verified main still has it and aborted rather than publish that.\n\nSo the union is a design decision, not a resolution: six tabs, the branch's five plus awaiting ratification, which needs the populations map to special-case a source that takes vocabulary and returns a different shape. That is real work on the UI, and it belongs to whoever holds the design, not to a rebase.\n\nThere is also a sequencing problem I should not paper over. Codex has promised a review of 43daa5f0 and has not reported. Carrying that head now means carrying a head that is about to change, and any changes codex requests would land on the old base and need carrying again. The cheaper order is to let that verdict land, then carry the reviewed content once.\n\nI have left no worktree, no branch and no candidate behind. Path ui is as the other lane left it.","body":{"attempted_carry_onto":"7e7b8412bcd95e3d3345a481b72febc502513109","blocking_commit":"75a1eb33","clean_commits":"4","collides_with_merged":"511335e7","outcome":"aborted, nothing published","source_head":"43daa5f03f3d662b7ab2ce83c63c05d753eb1aeb"}}